Added the config option ``qcodes.config.dataset.export_snapshot_in_group``. When enabled, the snapshot of datasets
exported to NetCDF is stored as a variable in the ``qcodes_metadata`` group, compressed with the same
``qcodes.config.dataset.export_netcdf_compression_level`` as the data, rather than as the
``snapshot`` attribute. The snapshot is then only read when needed, which reduces the time it takes to open
files with large snapshots, and their size when compression is enabled.
The ``snapshot`` attribute then contains a pointer to that location. ``load_from_netcdf`` supports both layouts, and
the new function ``qcodes.dataset.snapshot_from_netcdf`` can be used to read the snapshot from either layout
without a QCoDeS database. The option is disabled by default since tools that read the ``snapshot`` attribute directly
must be updated to support the new layout.
